  "title": "80: Abasa عبس",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nعَبَسَ وَتَوَلّٰٓىۙ‏(1)\nA’BASA WA TAWALLAA.\nHe frowned and turned away\nاَنْ جَآءَهُ الْاَعْمٰىؕ‏(2)\nAN JAAA-AHUL A-A’MAA.\nwhen the blind man approached him.\nوَمَا يُدْرِيْكَ لَعَلَّهٗ يَزَّكّٰٓىۙ‏(3)\nWA MAA YUDREEKA LA-A’LLAHU YAZZAKKAA.\nAnd how do you know, maybe he would purify himself,\nاَوْ يَذَّكَّرُ فَتَنْفَعَهُ الذِّكْرٰىؕ‏(4)\nAW YAZZAKKARO FATANFA-A’HUZ ZIKRAA.\nor take admonition, and the admonition would benefit him!\nاَمَّا مَنِ اسْتَغْنٰىۙ‏(5)\nAMMAA MANIS TAGHNAA.\nBut as for someone who is wealthy,\nفَاَنْتَ لَهٗ تَصَدّٰىؕ‏(6)\nFA-ANTA LAHU TASADDAA.\nyou attend to him,\nوَمَا عَلَيْكَ اَلَّا يَزَّكّٰٓىؕ‏(7)\nWA MAA A’LAYKA ALLAA YAZZAKKAA.\nthough you are not liable if he does not purify himself.\nوَاَمَّا مَنْ جَآءَكَ يَسْعٰىۙ‏(8)\nWA AMMAA MAN JAAA-A-KA YAS-A’A.\nBut as for someone who comes hurrying to you,\nوَهُوَ يَخْشٰىۙ‏(9)\nWA HOWA YAKHSHAA.\nwhile he fears [Allah],\nفَاَنْتَ عَنْهُ تَلَهّٰى‌ۚ‏(10)\nFA-ANTA A’NHO TALAHHAA.\nyou are neglectful of him.\nكَلَّاۤ اِنَّهَا تَذْكِرَةٌ ۚ‏(11)\nKALLAA INNAHAA TAZKERAH.\nNo indeed! These [verses of the Quran ] are a reminder\nفَمَنْ شَآءَ ذَكَرَهٗ‌ۘ‏(12)\nFAMAN SHAA-A ZAKARAH.\n—so let anyone who wishes remember—\nفِىْ صُحُفٍ مُّكَرَّمَةٍۙ‏(13)\nFEE SOHOFIM MOKARRAMATIM.\nin honoured scriptures,\nمَّرْفُوْعَةٍ مُّطَهَّرَةٍ ۭۙ‏(14)\nMARFOO-A’TIM MOTAHHARATIM.\nexalted and purified,\nبِاَيْدِىْ سَفَرَةٍۙ‏(15)\nBE-AYDEE SAFARATIN.\nin the hands of envoys,\nكِرَامٍۢ بَرَرَةٍؕ‏(16)\nKERAAMIM BARARAH.\nnoble and pious.\nقُتِلَ الْاِنْسَانُ مَاۤ اَكْفَرَهٗؕ‏(17)\nQOTELAL INSAANO MAA AKFARAH.\nPerish man! How ungrateful is he!\nمِنْ اَىِّ شَىْءٍ خَلَقَهٗؕ‏(18)\nMIN  AYYE SHAY-IN KHALAQAH.\nFrom what did He create him?\nمِنْ نُّطْفَةٍؕ خَلَقَهٗ فَقَدَّرَهٗ ۙ‏(19)\nMIN NUTFAH, KHALAQAHU FAQADDARAHU.\nHe created him from a drop of [seminal] fluid; then proportioned him.\nثُمَّ السَّبِيْلَ يَسَّرَهٗۙ‏(20)\nSUMMAS SABEELA YASSARAHU.\nThen He made the way easy for him;\nثُمَّ اَمَاتَهٗ فَاَقْبَرَهٗۙ‏(21)\nSUMMA AMAATAHU FA-AQBARAHU.\nthen He made him die and buried him;\nثُمَّ اِذَا شَآءَ اَنْشَرَهٗؕ‏(22)\nSUMMA EZAA SHAA-A ANSHARAH.\nand then, when He wished, resurrected him.\nكَلَّا لَمَّا يَقْضِ مَاۤ اَمَرَهٗؕ‏(23)\nKALLAA LAMMAA YAQZE MAA AMARAH.\nNo indeed! He has not yet carried out what He has commanded him.\nفَلْيَنْظُرِ الْاِنْسَانُ اِلٰى طَعَامِهٖۤۙ‏(24)\nFAL-YANZORIL INSAANO ELAA TA-A’AMEH.\nLet man consider his food:\nاَنَّا صَبَبْنَا الْمَآءَ صَبًّا ۙ‏(25)\nANNAA SABABNAL MAAA-A SABBAA.\nWe pour down plenteous water [from the sky],\nثُمَّ شَقَقْنَا الْاَرْضَ شَقًّا ۙ‏(26)\nSUMMA SHAQAQNAN ARZA SHAQQAA.\nthen We split the earth making fissures in it\nفَاَنْۢبَتْنَا فِيْهَا حَبًّا ۙ‏(27)\nFA-ANBATNAA FEEHAA HABBANW.\nand make the grain grow in it,\nوَّ عِنَبًا وَّقَضْبًا ۙ‏(28)\nWA E’NABANW WA QAZBANW.\nas well as vines and vegetables,\nوَّزَيْتُوْنًا وَّنَخْلًا ؕ‏(29)\nWA ZAYTOONANW WA NAKHLANW.\nolives and date palms,\nوَحَدَآئِقَ غُلْبًا ۙ‏(30)\nWA HADAAA-EQA GULBANW.\nand densely-planted gardens,\nوَّفَاكِهَةً وَّاَبًّا ۙ‏(31)\nWA FAAKEHATNW WA ABBAM.\nfruits and pastures,\nمَّتَاعًا لَّكُمْ وَلِاَنْعَامِكُمْؕ‏(32)\nMATAA-A’L LAKUM WA LE-ANA’AMEKUM.\nas a sustenance for you and your livestock.\nفَاِذَا جَآءَتِ الصَّآخَّةُ‏(33)\nFE-EZAA JAAA-ATIS SAAAKHKHAH.\nSo when the deafening Cry comes—\nيَوْمَ يَفِرُّ الْمَرْءُ مِنْ اَخِيْهِۙ‏(34)\nYAWMA YAFIRRUL MAR-O MIN AKHEEHE.\nthe day when a man will evade his brother,\nوَاُمِّهٖ وَاَبِيْهِۙ‏(35)\nWA UMMEHI WA ABEEHE.\nhis mother and his father,\nوَصَاحِبَتِهٖ وَبَنِيْهِؕ‏(36)\nWA SAAHEBATEHI WA BANEEHE.\nhis spouse and his sons—\nلِكُلِّ امْرِیءٍ مِّنْهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ شَاْنٌ يُّغْنِيْهِؕ‏(37)\nLEKULLIM RE-IM MINHUM YAWMA-EZIN SHAA-NUY YUGHNEEH.\neach of them will have a task to keep him preoccupied on that day.\nوُجُوْهٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ مُّسْفِرَةٌ ۙ‏(38)\nWOJOOHINY YAWMA-EZIM MUSFERATUN.\nSome faces will be bright on that day,\nضَاحِكَةٌ مُّسْتَبْشِرَةٌ ۚ‏(39)\nZAAHEKATUM MUSTABSHERAH.\nlaughing and joyous,\nوَوُجُوْهٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ عَلَيْهَا غَبَرَةٌ ۙ‏(40)\nWA WOJOOHINY YAWMA-EZIN A’LAYHAA GHABARATUN.\nand some faces on that day will be covered with dust,\nتَرْهَقُهَا قَتَرَةٌ ؕ‏(41)\nTARHAQOHAA QATARAH.\novercast with gloom.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْكَفَرَةُ الْفَجَرَةُ‏(42)\nOOLAAA-EKA HOMUL KAFARATUL FAJARAH.\nIt is they who are the faithless, the vicious.",
  "merits": "Surah Abasa (He Frowned)\nThis Surah has 42 verses and it was revealed in Makkah. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the person who recites this Surah will come out of his grave laughing on the Day of Resurrection.\nWriting this Surah as a talisman on deerskin and keeping it in one’s possession makes one successful in all his endeavours. If it is recited during a journey, then the traveller will return home safely. Whoever recites this Surah with [Surah at-Takweer](A85) will be under the shade of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) in Jannah."
